<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Governorate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as gubernii, governorates</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A governorate (guberniya) was the main administrative unit of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, headed by a governor appointed by the tsar. The system was reorganised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a> in 1775, and it remained the basis of Russian provincial government until the revolution.</p></div>
